WEBVTT

00:14.760 --> 00:18.220
Five years ago, we expelled him

00:18.220 --> 00:22.160
and barred him from obtaining 
a detective's license.

00:30.590 --> 00:33.500
We at BLUE seek the truth.

00:33.500 --> 00:38.720
And to ensure that justice is never 
overshadowed by evil, we train detectives.

00:38.720 --> 00:41.830
We cannot have a detective who kills people.

00:42.180 --> 00:45.730
To determine whether he 
has resumed detective work,

00:45.730 --> 00:49.270
it is necessary to determine 
the veracity of this information.

00:52.290 --> 00:54.330
I believe I'm suited to the task.

00:57.390 --> 00:58.830
Very well.

00:58.830 --> 01:00.760
I will entrust this to you.

01:00.760 --> 01:04.760
I officially order an investigation 
of Kamonohashi Ron.

01:05.370 --> 01:09.770
Our goal is nothing more
 than to verify the intel we've received.

01:09.770 --> 01:14.040
Agitate him, and you risk
 granting him an opportunity to flee.

01:14.610 --> 01:17.990
Refrain from direct contact as much as possible.

01:18.640 --> 01:21.230
Even if you catch him in the act of sleuthing,

01:21.230 --> 01:23.350
you are to report back first.

01:23.350 --> 01:25.180
Understood.

01:33.010 --> 01:39.200
And if he truly is acting as a detective, 
what do you intend to do?

01:39.600 --> 01:41.430
That should be evident.

01:41.430 --> 01:45.280
We cannot allow such tragedy
to happen again.

01:45.280 --> 01:48.120
Kamonohashi Ron's crimes are clear.

01:50.130 --> 01:53.060
If the intel we've received is true,

01:53.460 --> 01:56.560
there is but one punishment to hand down.

02:09.210 --> 02:12.570
Ron    Kamonohashi's

02:09.210 --> 02:12.570
<i>Forbidden\h\h\h
</i>Deductions

03:26.970 --> 03:32.190
<b>#03   The Case of the Benizome Hot Spring Murder (Part 1)</b>

03:40.130 --> 03:41.220
Hello?

03:42.860 --> 03:43.950
What?!

03:44.320 --> 03:46.330
<b>Home Improvement Center</b>

03:53.250 --> 03:54.360
Ron!

03:54.890 --> 03:56.420
You said there's an emergency?!

03:57.090 --> 03:58.630
They won't let me start a tab.

03:58.630 --> 04:01.020
That is <i>not</i> an emergency!

04:01.840 --> 04:04.260
Sorry, but could you pay for me?

04:01.840 --> 04:04.260
<b>!!SALE!!</b>

04:04.260 --> 04:06.860
Don't call me for stuff like this...

04:06.860 --> 04:09.430
I thought BLUE was after 
your life or something.

04:09.740 --> 04:11.990
A cat's life is on the line.

04:11.990 --> 04:14.140
The cat is important, but...

04:14.140 --> 04:16.760
I mean, of course they 
won't let you start a tab.

04:14.370 --> 04:21.240
<b>Delicious Food</b>

04:14.370 --> 04:21.240
<b>Rich</b>

04:14.370 --> 04:21.240
<b>Additive-free</b>

04:16.760 --> 04:18.420
How've you lived up until now?

04:18.420 --> 04:21.240
People from the apartments bring me things.

04:21.240 --> 04:23.240
<b>Pet Toys</b>

04:21.240 --> 04:23.240
<b>Second Most Popular</b>

04:23.240 --> 04:25.450
<b>yen</b>

04:23.240 --> 04:25.450
<b>Total</b>

04:27.160 --> 04:29.870
Thank you for your patronage!

04:30.570 --> 04:33.940
We're currently running a raffle.

04:33.940 --> 04:38.880
We're handing out tickets
to customers with purchases.

04:38.340 --> 04:40.550
<b>Raffle Ticket</b>

04:38.880 --> 04:40.550
Please take one if you'd like.

04:43.510 --> 04:45.180
Th-Thank you...

04:45.180 --> 04:46.620
You're overdoing the gratitude there.

04:49.220 --> 04:53.180
<b>Huge Raffle Happening Now!</b>

04:49.220 --> 04:53.180
<b>Don't miss it!</b>

04:49.220 --> 04:53.180
<b>Your chance to win luxurious prizes!!!</b>

04:53.180 --> 04:58.150
<b>Consolation Prize: Pocket Tissues</b>

04:53.180 --> 04:58.150
<b>Fourth: Wireless Speaker</b>

04:53.180 --> 04:58.150
<b>Third: Air Circulator (Talk of the town!)</b>

04:53.180 --> 04:58.150
<b>High-End Cordless Vacuum</b>

04:53.180 --> 04:58.150
<b>Second: Hot Spring Vacation Voucher</b>

04:53.180 --> 04:58.150
<b>First: Hot Spring Vacation Vouchers <i>for Two</i></b>

05:00.930 --> 05:03.030
Okay, step right up!

05:03.030 --> 05:04.720
Thank you.

05:04.720 --> 05:06.820
Now give this a single spin.

05:06.820 --> 05:08.260
Just one, huh?

05:08.260 --> 05:11.310
To decide who'll do it, we'll play
a round of rock, paper, scissors.

05:11.310 --> 05:12.920
It's fine. Just spin it.

05:12.920 --> 05:15.200
Much obliged. I'd be happy to.

05:15.620 --> 05:18.330
My, you seem raring to go, young man.

05:32.430 --> 05:33.390
Huh?

05:35.410 --> 05:39.800
We have a winner!
The grand prize is a hot spring vacation!

05:39.800 --> 05:43.280
It's perfect for you two.
It happens to be a couple's package.

05:43.280 --> 05:45.140
You've got the absolute wrong idea about us!

05:45.140 --> 05:48.360
I spun for it, so I'll go twice.

05:48.360 --> 05:50.320
You can't do that.

05:50.320 --> 05:54.000
They're for a fixed date,
and reawarding them would be tragic.

05:54.000 --> 05:56.740
If you two won't go,
then we'll just cancel them.

05:58.320 --> 05:59.720
Guess we have no choice.

06:00.180 --> 06:01.040
Guess not.

06:01.040 --> 06:04.760
Man, today's really been something.

06:04.760 --> 06:08.200
We've handed out both the grand
and second-place prizes.

06:08.470 --> 06:10.430
Isshiki Totomaru

06:08.470 --> 06:10.430
Pure, naïve detective

06:12.390 --> 06:15.840
Thank you so much! Come again!

06:16.250 --> 06:18.620
If there's no case, then thanks and bye-bye.

06:18.620 --> 06:20.690
I can't believe you'd just 
cast me aside like that!

06:23.800 --> 06:25.400
A hot spring, huh?

06:38.220 --> 06:42.000
You fellas have incredible luck!

06:42.000 --> 06:45.530
It was pouring rain at Benizome 
Hot Spring up until yesterday.

06:45.530 --> 06:46.800
Really?

06:46.800 --> 06:51.010
But as you can see, 
today the weather is lovely.

06:51.010 --> 06:54.900
Oh, I have a pamphlet for the inn. 
Here, you can have it.

06:55.470 --> 06:56.820
Oh, thank you.

06:57.340 --> 07:02.910
Do you fellas know how this
 hot spring got its name, "Benizome"?

07:02.910 --> 07:03.940
No.

07:03.940 --> 07:08.130
Long ago, the fall leaves on the mountain 
turned a certain crimson called "beni,"

07:08.130 --> 07:13.550
and a lord who saw it reflected 
in the hot spring gave it that name.

07:12.900 --> 07:18.160
<b>Benizome Hot Spring</b>

07:13.550 --> 07:15.410
A charming story, isn't it?

07:15.410 --> 07:18.160
Wow. I'm really looking forward to this.

07:18.160 --> 07:19.870
<b>Main Building</b>

07:22.480 --> 07:25.400
The main building? 
We won tickets for the annex building.

07:28.550 --> 07:31.030
Th-The annex?!

07:31.030 --> 07:34.290
In that case, you want this one. 
I'm really sorry.

07:34.290 --> 07:35.740
Why are you apologizing?

07:36.060 --> 07:40.190
Because we made the pamphlet 
for the annex ourselves.

07:40.190 --> 07:41.610
I really am sorry.

07:41.610 --> 07:43.190
Seriously, why are you apologizing?

07:43.190 --> 07:45.270
A single black and white photocopy?

08:00.500 --> 08:02.320
Well, this is where I leave you!

08:05.930 --> 08:07.640
He left as quickly as he could.

08:07.640 --> 08:09.460
This is a very interesting inn.

08:13.930 --> 08:16.420
It's like a typhoon hit just this one spot.

08:13.930 --> 08:21.140
Benizome Annex

08:16.720 --> 08:18.800
Even the rain gutter's busted.

08:18.800 --> 08:20.190
Are they really open?

08:20.190 --> 08:21.500
Welcome!

08:21.500 --> 08:24.560
You have reservations under 
Nanban-sama and Isshiki-sama, correct?

08:24.560 --> 08:25.350
They <i>are</i> open!

08:27.560 --> 08:30.030
Welcome to the Benizome annex,

08:30.030 --> 08:31.990
Isshiki Totomaru-sama

08:32.410 --> 08:34.450
and Nanban Kamoo-sama.

08:34.810 --> 08:35.880
What's this?

08:35.880 --> 08:39.160
Thank you for your service
with the police force, Isshiki-sama.

08:39.660 --> 08:41.870
What? How did you know I'm with the police?

08:41.870 --> 08:43.830
Your shoes.

08:43.830 --> 08:46.710
The leather of the toes is scuffed.

08:46.710 --> 08:49.780
That only happens if you run all-out in them.

08:50.160 --> 08:53.200
And the only professionals
 who run in their leather shoes

08:53.540 --> 08:56.010
are police detectives
 chasing down criminals, I think.

08:56.010 --> 08:58.080
What an amazing deduction!

08:58.080 --> 08:59.750
Don't be fooled, Toto.

08:59.750 --> 09:00.720
What?

09:02.420 --> 09:02.920
Ow!

09:02.920 --> 09:05.360
When it comes to professionals
 running in leather shoes,

09:05.360 --> 09:06.940
I think a reporter might be just as likely.

09:06.940 --> 09:09.650
You only knew that
through our reservations.

09:09.650 --> 09:10.900
Isshiki Totomaru

09:09.650 --> 09:10.900
Pure, naïve detective

09:13.750 --> 09:16.360
It's just a little welcoming trick.
Do pardon me.

09:16.360 --> 09:17.670
See?

09:17.670 --> 09:19.070
Oh, I see.

09:19.380 --> 09:21.540
Now, please come inside.

09:28.270 --> 09:30.270
<b>Phone Box</b>

09:30.270 --> 09:31.960
Benizome Hot Spring

09:32.470 --> 09:34.330
The open-air bath is free-flowing,

09:34.330 --> 09:37.080
and you're welcome to use it 
anytime up until 8 AM tomorrow.

09:37.080 --> 09:40.680
Dinner will be served tonight at 7 PM. 
Please come to the Beni Room.

09:40.680 --> 09:43.150
With dinner at a predetermined time,

09:43.150 --> 09:45.730
does that mean there are 
other guests staying here?

09:45.730 --> 09:49.670
Yes. Today, we have three parties with us.

09:49.670 --> 09:50.900
Really?

09:50.900 --> 09:55.960
So we would very much appreciate it 
if you weren't late to dinner.

09:55.960 --> 09:57.170
All right.

09:57.780 --> 09:58.750
Ow!

09:59.060 --> 10:00.870
Please enjoy your stay.

10:00.870 --> 10:02.930
There're more people here than I thought.

10:03.940 --> 10:05.780
Should we hit the bath first?

10:05.780 --> 10:06.800
Yeah, let's.

10:08.430 --> 10:11.030
<i>That insight!</i>

10:11.030 --> 10:14.670
<i>He is, without a doubt, Kamonohashi Ron!</i>

10:20.780 --> 10:25.330
Wow, this bath is really impressive!

10:25.330 --> 10:27.830
I mean, getting to soak
while overlooking the river...

10:27.830 --> 10:29.230
It's not bad at all.

10:29.230 --> 10:32.650
The building's a wreck, 
but the bath is the best!

10:32.650 --> 10:35.620
If only it were stained crimson, 
it would be perfect.

10:35.620 --> 10:37.360
Like the story the cab driver told?

10:37.360 --> 10:40.930
That's just what they tell the public. 
There's also a secret legend.

10:40.930 --> 10:41.840
A secret one?

10:42.200 --> 10:46.460
As you can see,
the river has steps and runs swift.

10:46.460 --> 10:48.530
They say it often overflows.

10:48.530 --> 10:53.430
This caused problems for the villagers, 
so they sacrificed a young lady to it.

10:53.430 --> 10:55.920
The next day, the floodwater receded,

10:55.920 --> 11:00.680
but they say that for days afterward,
the river and hot spring ran crimson.

11:00.680 --> 11:02.890
Where'd you hear that terrifying story?

11:02.890 --> 11:05.080
It was in that pamphlet earlier.

11:05.490 --> 11:07.220
The one the driver made?

11:07.220 --> 11:09.600
Well, we don't exactly want 
the water running red.

11:09.600 --> 11:11.060
Of course we don't!

11:11.060 --> 11:12.810
Your face is saying the opposite!

11:15.600 --> 11:18.470
That tattoo is bigger than I thought it was.

11:19.490 --> 11:20.820
You mean this scar?

11:20.820 --> 11:22.320
It's a scar?

11:22.320 --> 11:25.070
I once suffered injuries all over my body,

11:25.070 --> 11:27.340
yet this was the only one that scarred.

11:27.340 --> 11:29.540
It looks like some kind of symbol or number.

11:29.540 --> 11:32.690
Yeah. I like it because there's a six in it.

11:32.690 --> 11:33.500
Six?

11:33.500 --> 11:36.730
A number I associate with my birth.

11:37.080 --> 11:39.460
Toto, you're your grandma's boy, so you'd like

11:38.170 --> 11:41.630
<b>Grandma</b>

11:39.460 --> 11:41.630
a scar that read "Grandma", wouldn't you?

11:41.630 --> 11:43.840
Can't I choose something else?!

11:46.560 --> 11:48.520
Beni Room

11:48.520 --> 11:50.820
I can't wait to see what they're serving.

11:50.820 --> 11:51.420
Yeah.

11:51.420 --> 11:52.400
Did you wash your hands?

11:52.400 --> 11:53.520
Are you tired?

11:55.980 --> 11:57.520
Yes, this is a nice place, isn't it?

11:57.520 --> 11:58.190
It is.

11:59.210 --> 12:03.120
Thank you for waiting.
Here's the dish you requested.

12:03.120 --> 12:04.030
Thanks.

12:05.870 --> 12:07.230
What type of slime is that?!

12:07.230 --> 12:09.270
It's omurice covered in black sugar syrup.

12:09.270 --> 12:11.970
Right. You were drinking that the other day...

12:12.460 --> 12:15.690
It's the source of my brainpower.

12:15.690 --> 12:19.170
I also drink black sesame paste 
to ward off anemia.

12:19.170 --> 12:20.920
<b>Kuro</b>

12:20.920 --> 12:23.010
Are you in cahoots with some 
traditional sweets shop?

12:23.950 --> 12:25.210
Now then...

12:25.630 --> 12:29.470
Hey, this is pretty amazing! Look!

12:29.470 --> 12:30.560
Just a minute.

12:30.560 --> 12:31.670
Hurry up!

12:31.670 --> 12:34.440
You're always so impatient.

12:34.870 --> 12:36.660
Wow! You weren't kidding!

12:36.660 --> 12:38.430
This is amazing!

12:41.320 --> 12:45.630
Hmm, he said that there were four 
parties staying here in total,

12:45.630 --> 12:48.190
so it seems someone has yet to arrive.

12:48.190 --> 12:50.840
But five people is just perfect.

12:53.500 --> 12:55.270
For The Game of Life!

12:53.500 --> 12:57.330
<b>Every life has its ups and downs! Aim to be a millionaire!
The Game of Life</b>

12:53.500 --> 12:57.330
<b>Your choice of 4 different areas!</b>

12:55.270 --> 12:57.330
Is that what kept hitting me?!

12:57.330 --> 13:03.060
"Playing The Game of Life at a hot spring" is on
 the list I made in my five-year seclusion.

13:03.060 --> 13:05.050
I'm terrified to hear the rest of that list.

13:05.420 --> 13:07.940
Now, let's play! Let's play this instant!

13:07.940 --> 13:09.200
Wait! Hey!

13:11.830 --> 13:13.360
I'm so sorry.

13:13.360 --> 13:17.480
Everyone's in the middle of their meals!
We haven't finished eating either!

13:17.480 --> 13:20.730
Besides, you're supposed to play
 ping-pong at hot springs, right?

13:20.730 --> 13:22.080
Ping-pong, huh?

13:22.440 --> 13:24.690
I suppose I can save the fun for later.

13:24.690 --> 13:26.570
For now, let's just eat our dinner.

13:33.710 --> 13:35.620
The place is really going to ruin, huh?

13:42.240 --> 13:44.600
I've found something interesting, Toto.

13:44.600 --> 13:45.380
Huh?

13:45.930 --> 13:49.670
An old scroll that tells the secret 
story of the crimson hue.

13:50.100 --> 13:51.950
What a creepy drawing!

13:51.950 --> 13:57.060
Perhaps the death of a young woman 
really did dye all the waters red.

13:57.920 --> 13:59.510
Quite trying to scare me!

14:00.950 --> 14:02.890
I've found a ball and paddles.

14:02.890 --> 14:06.050
Since we're doing this, 
why don't we play with a special rule?

14:06.050 --> 14:07.570
A special rule?

14:07.570 --> 14:10.030
That's right. A very special rule.

14:10.540 --> 14:11.910
What is it?

14:12.240 --> 14:14.220
Whoever loses...

14:16.810 --> 14:20.130
has to be the winner's slave for life!

14:20.130 --> 14:22.160
Wha?! Hang on!

14:26.670 --> 14:28.380
Looks like I win.

14:28.380 --> 14:29.590
That wasn't fair.

14:33.300 --> 14:34.670
Is there a spare ball?

14:34.670 --> 14:35.810
I only found the one.

14:36.690 --> 14:37.950
We're going to get it.

14:46.940 --> 14:51.410
The ball floated off somewhere and 
I'm getting cold. Let's head to the bath.

14:51.410 --> 14:53.870
Don't forget that I won.

14:53.870 --> 14:59.060
Your first job as my slave is to steal
 unsolved case files from the station!

14:59.060 --> 15:00.280
Like I can do that!

15:04.880 --> 15:08.320
Ah, this really is paradise...

15:09.330 --> 15:12.850
Work just wouldn't end, 
and I had to walk from the station.

15:12.850 --> 15:14.820
It's already so late...

15:15.640 --> 15:19.160
But since I'm here, 
I think I'll refresh myself!

15:22.610 --> 15:25.820
Aim to be police superintendent general!

15:53.760 --> 15:57.660
Amamiya-senpai, I never imagined you were 
the one who won the second prize.

15:57.660 --> 15:59.920
Isshiki the fool is one thing,

15:59.920 --> 16:03.090
but to think even Kamoo-san 
went into the women's bath...

16:03.090 --> 16:05.230
Huh? That was the men's bath, wasn't it?

16:05.230 --> 16:06.730
Yeah. It was the men's bath.

16:07.080 --> 16:08.190
Wha?!

16:08.190 --> 16:09.150
<b>Men</b>

16:11.500 --> 16:14.610
<i>Kamoo-sama must think
 I'm some kind of pervert!</i>

16:15.870 --> 16:17.360
I want a divorce!

16:18.330 --> 16:21.710
Hey, that was just a joke. 
Don't take it so seriously.

16:21.710 --> 16:23.360
Even so, you...

16:23.360 --> 16:24.760
You can't!

16:24.760 --> 16:28.000
You can't get a divorce!

16:29.330 --> 16:31.510
Amamiya-senpai, are you a weepy drunk?

16:34.150 --> 16:35.240
I'm going to bed!

16:35.240 --> 16:36.240
Ma'am!

16:48.730 --> 16:51.820
Somehow, that took the wind out of my sails.

16:52.130 --> 16:55.660
Why don't you take a dip 
in the bath and refresh yourself?

16:55.660 --> 16:57.280
You haven't been yet, right?

16:57.280 --> 16:59.800
That's true. Thank you.

17:03.660 --> 17:06.130
I'm sorry for yelling at you.

17:06.130 --> 17:08.200
You just relax here, all right?

17:08.200 --> 17:09.200
I will.

17:13.760 --> 17:16.020
Seems you have some time
 on your hands, hubby.

17:16.470 --> 17:18.630
What do you say to playing The Game of Life?

17:16.470 --> 17:20.060
<b>Every life has its ups and downs! Aim to be a millionaire!
The Game of Life</b>

17:18.630 --> 17:20.060
Where were you hiding that?!

17:22.070 --> 17:23.520
Sounds like fun.

17:23.970 --> 17:25.400
How about you?

17:26.220 --> 17:28.590
Want a do-over on your tedious life?

17:28.590 --> 17:29.690
Don't be a jerk!

17:29.690 --> 17:32.790
Sure. I've got time. Might as well play.

17:43.640 --> 17:46.660
Sweet! My profession is entertainer!

17:47.920 --> 17:50.510
All right! I'm a multimillionaire!

17:50.510 --> 17:52.090
Kamoo, you're in last place!

17:52.090 --> 17:54.250
That's because I'm playing fair today.

17:54.250 --> 17:55.840
Wh-What does that mean?

17:57.490 --> 18:01.010
If only we could really 
do our lives over this way.

17:59.300 --> 18:01.010
<b>Your lie is exposed. Pay $10,000.</b>

17:59.300 --> 18:01.010
<b>You wished three times on a shooting star.
Receive $21,000.</b>

18:01.480 --> 18:04.470
I was just thinking the same thing.

18:07.170 --> 18:08.580
Are you sleepy?

18:08.580 --> 18:11.690
It's pretty late. 
Shall we call it a night now?

18:11.690 --> 18:13.070
I suppose we should.

18:13.070 --> 18:16.400
Here, multimillionaire. You can 
take all the paper money with you.

18:16.400 --> 18:18.030
You're telling me to clean up?!

18:46.880 --> 18:49.270
I'm a police officer. What's happened?

18:49.720 --> 18:52.520
I went into the women's bath 
to clean and there's someone...

18:53.480 --> 18:54.520
Toto.

18:54.910 --> 18:55.940
Yeah.

18:58.490 --> 18:59.810
That's...

19:12.670 --> 19:15.570
It's that man's wife.

19:15.570 --> 19:16.880
Sachiko.

19:16.880 --> 19:17.660
Sachiko!

19:17.660 --> 19:19.590
Sir! Get a hold of yourself!

19:19.590 --> 19:22.560
Sachiko? I thought you were sleeping...

19:23.460 --> 19:24.680
Senpai?

19:28.930 --> 19:31.250
Rigor mortis has begun to set in.

19:31.250 --> 19:33.020
That puts the time of death...

19:33.440 --> 19:36.120
sometime between midnight and 2 AM.

19:37.830 --> 19:39.280
Pardon me.

19:39.940 --> 19:42.660
I promise I will avenge you.

19:42.660 --> 19:44.870
K-Kamoo-san?

19:44.870 --> 19:47.330
<i>He's even doing that here?!</i>

19:48.100 --> 19:50.970
W-We can't have civilians 
entering the crime scene!

19:50.970 --> 19:55.170
There aren't any obvious external injuries, 
but something clearly isn't right.

19:55.560 --> 19:59.300
There weren't this many 
fallen leaves here last night.

19:59.690 --> 20:02.760
This crimson layer on the water... 
It's like that story.

20:03.120 --> 20:08.190
The one about the young sacrifice
that made the hot spring turn red.

20:08.190 --> 20:09.220
What if it's a curse?!

20:09.220 --> 20:10.560
Th-That can't be.

20:12.550 --> 20:14.210
What an interesting perspective.

20:14.210 --> 20:15.190
Huh?

20:15.190 --> 20:19.880
But Detective Isshiki here 
just can't stop doubting people.

20:22.220 --> 20:23.180
Isn't that right?

20:23.180 --> 20:24.180
Huh?

20:24.450 --> 20:26.160
Y-Yeah.

20:26.550 --> 20:31.630
Um, did you notice anything between 
the hours of midnight and 2 AM?

20:32.120 --> 20:35.950
Someone suspicious or a strange sound?
Anything at all.

20:36.270 --> 20:37.590
I'm sorry.

20:37.590 --> 20:40.170
Our in is small, so we take turns.

20:40.170 --> 20:43.670
There's only ever one
 of us on the night shift.

20:43.670 --> 20:45.300
And that was me.

20:47.260 --> 20:49.670
You were in the lounge.

20:49.670 --> 20:54.300
Yes. I was watching over all of you,
so I can provide a statement.

20:55.000 --> 20:58.060
I believe you all saw for yourselves

20:58.060 --> 21:01.700
that only one individual
returned to their room

21:01.700 --> 21:03.980
before the late missus left for hers.

21:07.700 --> 21:09.670
Isn't that right...

21:10.410 --> 21:12.140
Detective Amamiya?

21:15.870 --> 21:18.960
Now that you mention it, that's true.

21:18.960 --> 21:21.190
W-Wait just a minute, please!

21:21.190 --> 21:22.420
I remember that, too!

21:23.090 --> 21:24.630
So the one who did this is...

21:24.630 --> 21:26.840
There's no way it was her.

21:30.740 --> 21:31.760
It wasn't.

21:33.570 --> 21:35.940
Amamiya-kun isn't the culprit.

21:36.510 --> 21:39.520
It was someone else 
who's here with us right now.

21:43.250 --> 21:44.670
What are you saying?

21:44.670 --> 21:47.170
She left first.
That's a fact.

21:47.170 --> 21:48.490
I saw it, too.

21:48.930 --> 21:53.240
It's true that she's the only one
with an uncertain alibi.

21:53.240 --> 21:58.490
But the simple act of creating this 
situation was impossible for her.

22:01.500 --> 22:05.800
And I can prove it to you right now.
